maint binhost:
Generate binary package metadata index


maint binpkg:
Inspect/verify/prune local binary packages (em-only, no emaint equivalent)


maint cleanconfmem:
No-op: em keeps no config-memory file to go stale


maint cleanresume:
Discard saved resume lists
  -f, --fix  Actually delete the saved resume/resume-backup lists (default: just
             report what's there).


maint logs:
Prune the build.log files finished merges leave in the build tree
      --fix               Remove them; without this the logs are only listed
  -t, --older-than <AGE>  Only consider logs at least this old (e.g. `30d`,
                          `2weeks`)


maint merges:
Unavailable: em keeps no failed-merge registry


maint movebin:
Apply package moves to binary packages


maint moveinst:
Apply package moves to installed packages


maint regen-use:
Regenerate profiles/use.local.desc from metadata.xml
  -o, --output <PATH>  Write output here instead of profiles/use.local.desc ('-'
                       for stdout)


maint revisions:
Purge repo revision history from repo_revisions
  [REPO]…  Purge only these repos (default: all)


maint sync:
Sync repositories (git, rsync)
  [REPOS]…  Repo names from repos.conf (default: auto-sync enabled repos)


maint world:
Check (and optionally fix) problems in the world file
  -f, --fix  Remove orphaned entries from the world file

=== em maint binhost ===
Generate binary package metadata index

Usage: em maint binhost

Flags:
  -h, --help                Print help

Global flags:
      --color <WHEN>
                            [possible values: auto, always, never]
                            (default: auto)
  -p, --pretend             Show what would be done without actually performing
                            any actions
  -v, --verbose             Increase verbosity: `-v` labels each build phase,
                            `-vv`/`-vvv` add `em`'s own debug/trace logs (see
                            also `RUST_LOG`).
  -q, --quiet               Suppress non-error output
      --arch <ARCH>         Target architecture for operations (default: current
                            system architecture)
      --repo <PATH>         Pin search/query to a single repository

                            When unset, repositories are auto-discovered from
                            `repos.conf` (the main repo wins for single-repo
                            applets; search walks all of them).
      --prefix <DIR>        Unprivileged offset: ROOT/VDB/distfiles/build trees
                            under DIR; config still from the host (use --root
                            for a config offset).
      --local [DIR]         Unprivileged, standalone Gentoo-Prefix: own
                            VDB/BROOT/config, not overlaid on the host (see
                            --prefix for the overlay). Defaults to ~/.gentoo
                            (EPREFIX=~/.gentoo) when no DIR is given.
    Warning: em active --local set steals set as the directory. Put the
             subcommand first: em active set --local=
      --config-root <PATH>  Read config (profile, make.conf) from this root
                            instead of `--root`
      --vdb <PATH>          Override VDB path (default: $ROOT/var/db/pkg)
  -T, --target <TUPLE>      Cross-build/setup for a crossdev target tuple

                            The single source for "which tuple" everywhere: `em
                            crossdev --target T --init-target` sets T up; `em
                            stages --target T --stage1` (or any plain atom
                            build) resolves/installs into the target sysroot
                            `<EROOT>/usr/<TUPLE>` — sugar for `--config-root
                            <sysroot> --root <sysroot>`.

                            Cross context (CHOST/CBUILD, `--root-deps=rdeps`) is
                            read from the sysroot make.conf. One flag for both
                            roles — `crossdev` no longer has its own
                            `-t`/`--target`.
      --root <PATH>         Installation root (the offset an applet installs
                            into / queries)

=== em maint binpkg ===
Inspect/verify/prune local binary packages (em-only, no emaint equivalent)

Usage: em maint binpkg <SUBCOMMAND>

Commands:
  fingerprint  Print the build-env key for the current roots' make.conf flags
  gpg-import   Import an armored OpenPGP public key into the GPG verify keyring
  list         List indexed binary packages (cpv, build-id, size, path)
  prune        Keep only the newest BUILD_ID per package, deleting older ones
  verify       Check each indexed binpkg's size/MD5/SHA1 against the file on
               disk
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Flags:
  -h, --help                Print help

Global flags:
      --color <WHEN>
                            [possible values: auto, always, never]
                            (default: auto)
  -p, --pretend             Show what would be done without actually performing
                            any actions
  -v, --verbose             Increase verbosity: `-v` labels each build phase,
                            `-vv`/`-vvv` add `em`'s own debug/trace logs (see
                            also `RUST_LOG`).
