query belongs:
Find which package owns a file
  <FILE>…  File path(s) to look up in the VDB contents records


query check:
Verify checksums of installed package
  <ATOM>…  Installed package atom(s) to verify


query depends:
List packages depending on an atom
  <ATOM>…  Atom(s) whose dependents to list


query depgraph:
Display full dependency tree
  <ATOM>…  Atom(s) to resolve and display the dependency tree for
  -f, --format <FORMAT>  Output format
    [possible values: pretty, json, tree]
    (default: pretty)
      --autosolve-use    Let the solver choose USE flags to satisfy REQUIRED_USE
                         (Level C)
  -D, --deep             Re-examine transitive dependencies

                         With `--update` (`-uD`), upgrades installed packages in
                         the depgraph to the newest accepted in-slot version
                         (emerge `-uD`). Alone, still bumps `:*` any-slot deps
                         to the newest slot rather than keeping a satisfying
                         installed slot.
  -N, --newuse           Reinstall installed packages when their planned USE or
                         IUSE differs from the VDB (emerge `--newuse`)

                         Applies to packages that appear in the depgraph; pairs
                         with `--deep` for a full-tree USE recheck.
  -U, --changed-use      Like `--newuse`, but only rebuild when an *enabled* USE
                         flag changed among flags present in both installed and
                         current IUSE (ignore pure IUSE add/drop). Emerge's
                         `--changed-use` / `-U`.
  -e, --emptytree        Treat every atom as not-yet-installed (emerge's
                         `-e`/`--emptytree`)
  -o, --onlydeps         Only show dependencies, excluding the given atoms
                         themselves from the tree
      --with-bdeps       Include build-time dependencies (BDEPEND) in the
                         resolution
      --root-deps        emerge's `--root-deps[=rdeps]`: only require RDEPEND
                         (not DEPEND) to be satisfiable in the merge target.


query files:
List files installed by a package
  <ATOM>…  Atom(s) whose installed file list to show


query has:
List installed packages by a VDB field value
  <FIELD>  VDB field to match, e.g. `SLOT`, `USE`, `repository`
  [VALUE]  Value the field must contain; omit to list every package whose field
           is set at all


query hasuse:
List packages with a given USE flag in IUSE
  <FLAG>…  USE flag name(s) to search for in IUSE


query keywords:
Display keyword status across architectures
  <ATOM>…  Atom(s) to show keyword status for


query list:
List installed/available packages matching a pattern
  [PATTERN]…  Glob or substring pattern(s); omit to list all packages
  -I, --installed  List only installed packages (from VDB), not available ones


query meta:
Display package metadata (maintainer, homepage, etc.)
  <ATOM>…  Atom(s) whose metadata to display


query size:
Display total file size of a package
  <ATOM>…  Atom(s) whose installed file size to sum


query uses:
Display USE flags for a package
  <ATOM>…  Atom(s) whose USE flags to display


query which:
Print full path to the ebuild for a package
  <ATOM>…  Atom(s) to resolve to an ebuild path


Examples:
    $ em query depgraph zlib
    $ em query belongs /usr/bin/python
    $ em query list -I

